Hey Henrik,

Thanks a lot for your help but the student I am trying to help has managed to find a copy of the data they need to work with pre normalised so has decided not attempt to normalise the data anymore.

Cheers for all your help though.

Saif

On Tuesday, 28 February 2012 11:46:36 UTC, Saif UrRehman wrote:
> Hi guys,
>
> I am trying to normalise 5000 HG-U133A celfiles using the aroma library it seems to run fine.
>
> However it stopped reading in Celfiles after 2,246 files after about 11 hours. It appears to fail silently.
>
>
> The code used was as follows:
>
> setwd("path")
> library(aroma.affymetrix)
> verbose <- Arguments$getVerbose(-8, timestamp=TRUE)
> chipType <- "HG-U133A"
> cdf <- AffymetrixCdfFile$byChipType(chipType)
> print(cdf)
> cs <- AffymetrixCelSet$byName("CELFILES", cdf=cdf)
> print(cs)
> bc <- RmaBackgroundCorrection(cs)
> csBC <- process(bc,verbose=verbose)
>
>
> The code appears to conclude but on inspection it only placed 2,246 files in the output probeData/ folder.
>
> I was wondering if anyone had encountered a similar problem and what solutions they found?
>
> Thanks a lot in advance.
>
> Sincerely,
> Saif Ur-Rehman
